title: Example - Markdown image - external URL
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown

**Pattern:** `![tooltip](https://...)` — the source is a plain URL, no tiddler involved.

The [IMAGE marker tiddler](#vocab/markdown/IMAGE) emits a `<$image source="https://...">` widget. TW's image widget detects that the source isn't a known tiddler title and treats it as a URL, generating `<img src="https://...">` directly.

**Live example:**

![TiddlyWiki favicon](https://tiddlywiki.com/favicon.ico)

**Source:**

```
![TiddlyWiki favicon](https://tiddlywiki.com/favicon.ico)
```

**Why this works:** TW's image widget first calls `wiki.getTiddler(source)`. For `https://tiddlywiki.com/favicon.ico` no such tiddler exists, so the widget falls through to the "URL" branch and uses the source string verbatim as the `<img src>`.

**Accessibility fallback:** since the URL isn't a tiddler, `attr-alt-from` / `attr-tooltip-from` find nothing to read and leave their attributes unset. The body-attribute `tooltip` then takes effect: the bracketed `TiddlyWiki favicon` text becomes the `tooltip` (rendered as the DOM `title` attribute). The DOM `alt` ends up unset — for external URLs that you want screen-reader-accessible, write a meaningful body. (A future enhancement could mirror body to `alt` automatically for the external-URL case.)

**Related:**

- [Source is a tiddler whose _canonical_uri is the URL — same external fetch, plus alt-text field for accessibility](#Example - Markdown image - canonical URI)
